"<header class=\"topbar\">\n    <div class=\"wrap\">\n      <a class=\"wordmark\" href=\"/\" aria-label=\"Lotolipi home\">lotolipi<span>.</span></a>\n      <nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"/\">Home</a><a href=\"/#case-studies\">Case studies</a><a href=\"/lottolov\">Lottolov</a><a href=\"/resume\">Résumé</a><a href=\"/#contact\">Contact</a></nav>\n    </div>\n  </header><main id=\"main-content\"><section class=\"hero wrap\"><p class=\"label\"><a href=\"/#case-studies\">Case studies</a> / Visitor experience</p><h1>Field Guide<span>.</span></h1><p class=\"hero-intro\">A visitor has 45 minutes, two interests and a whole exhibition to explore. How can they make room for a discovery along the way?</p><a class=\"hero-link\" href=\"/field-guide/index.html\">Plan a visit →</a></section><section class=\"work\"><div class=\"wrap\"><header class=\"work-head\"><p class=\"label\">Independent concept · Fictional exhibition</p><h2>A route with room to change.</h2><p>I designed a single-floor exhibition with twelve exhibits across three galleries. A route starts with the visitor’s interests, time budget and access preferences.</p></header><img src=\"/field-guide/floor.svg\" width=\"600\" height=\"300\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" alt=\"Cloth, Impression and Object galleries share a corridor\"><div class=\"walkthrough-copy\"><h3>Show where the time goes.</h3><p>Each numbered stop names its gallery, its subject, the walk to get there and the viewing time. The planner first tries to represent both interests, then fills the remaining time with up to four stops. The step-free filter excludes the raised displays.</p><h3>Make the detour a choice.</h3><p>Try the default textiles and printmaking route. Give the indigo loom ten more minutes. Before you commit, the guide names the stop you would lose. One action restores the original route.</p><h3>What remains to learn</h3><p>Walking and viewing times are illustrative. A visitor study would test whether people understand the trade-off before they change the route and whether the timing feels realistic on the floor.</p><a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"/field-guide/index.html\">Try the route planner →</a></div></div></section></main>"